      "problem": "Rewrite the expression $({x}^{2}-8x+16)-2$ as the difference between a perfect square and a constant.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we recall the following formula:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2ax+{a}^{2}=(x-a)^{2}\n$$\n\nNotice that we have a perfect square in the parentheses that we can factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x+16 & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-8x+{4}^{2} & = \\\\ {x}^{2}-2\\cdot 4x+{4}^{2} & = \\\\ (x-4)^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}-8x+16)-2 & = \\\\ (x-4)^{2}-2 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
